<Ui>
    <!--
        The OPTIONS window (decision 0950) — slice A: the shell. Opened from the game menu's
        Options button; the pages themselves (setting rows backed by real benilla knobs) come in
        the next slice, so the page body ships EMPTY and Defaults ships disabled.

        This window is the one deliberate era-1.15.9 skin in a 1.12 shell (0950): the 1.12
        OptionsFrame family (four separate panels) collapses into the era SettingsPanel look —
        one window, a category list, one page area. Ground truth is the era dump
        (wow-ui-source-era @ 1.15.9.68940), transcribed via the session's reference spec:
        · **Root** — Blizzard_SettingsPanel.xml `SettingsPanel`: 920x724, CENTER, strata HIGH,
          hidden. Skin per `SettingsFrameTemplate` (Classic/Blizzard_SettingsPanelTemplates.xml):
          FlatPanelBackgroundTemplate at TOPLEFT (7,-18) → BOTTOMRIGHT (-3,3), the
          `ButtonFrameTemplateNoPortrait` nine-slice (Classic/NineSliceLayouts.lua l.132 — right
          edge x=-8/x1=8), the `_UI-Frame-TitleTileBg` title band (256x17, TexCoords
          .2890625/.421875, TOPLEFT (8,-3) → TOPRIGHT (0,-3)), title GameFontNormal TOP (0,-5).
        · **Category list** — Blizzard_CategoryList.xml + .lua: rows/headers STRETCH to the
          scroll target's width (199, no scroll bar); header 30 tall (label 14px white at
          LEFT (20,-1), Options_CategoryHeader_<n> wash at TOPLEFT at atlas size, n cycling
          per header); row 20 tall (label GameFontNormal TOPLEFT (36,+1); bg CENTER —
          options_list_active selected / options_list_hover hover, at atlas size); 2 between
          elements, 18-tall spacer between groups (so 22 row-to-header).
        · **Page area** — Blizzard_SettingsList.xml: title 20px white TOPLEFT (7,-22), the
          options_horizontaldivider at TOP (0,-50), Defaults 96x22 at TOPRIGHT (-36,-16).
        · **Tabs** — SharedXML Shared/Tabs/MinimalTab.{xml,lua}: a bottom-anchored three-slice
          of Options_Tab[_Active]_{Left,Middle,Right}, GameTab TOPLEFT (32,-27) h37, AddOnsTab
          5 right of it; width text+40; selected = white small text at BOTTOM+6, unselected =
          gold small at BOTTOM+4.
        · **Search box** — SharedXML SearchBoxTemplate → InputBoxVisualTemplate
          (SecureUIPanelTemplates.xml l.42-67): the common-search-border three-slice (8x20 caps,
          left hung 5 outside, middle stretched, all centered on the 22 box), 10x10 magnifier at
          LEFT (1,-1), 17x17 clear button at RIGHT (-3), TextInsets 16/20, instructions label
          GameFontDisableSmall tinted 0.35 at TOPLEFT (16,0) → BOTTOMRIGHT (-20,0).
        Atlas members resolve by name through WoW-era/_extracted_ui/manifest.json (the 0950
        seam); era-only FILE textures ride the same extraction as `era:textures/<fdid>.blp`.

        SCOPE / divergences (noted, not bugs):
        - **horizTile/vertTile are unsupported**, so every repeating tile is STRETCHED for now:
          the `_UI-Frame-TitleTile` top band (a 256x28 repeat), the title-bg band under it, the
          `!UI-Frame-LeftTile`/`!UI-Frame-RightTile` columns and the `_UI-Frame-Bot` strip. At
          this window's spans the stretch reads as a soft smear of the tile — the gap to close
          when tiling lands.
        - **FlatPanelBackgroundTemplate is ONE solid fill here.** The era template is four
          textures (two rounded-corner atlas pieces + two fills) all tinted the engine-side
          global PANEL_BACKGROUND_COLOR = (0.122, 0.118, 0.129, 0.8) — the constant is defined in
          the client binary, not the Lua dump; value read off the GlobalColor db2 mirror
          (warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/ColorMixin). One flat quad loses only the 16px rounded bottom
          corners. The "lighter inner panel" on top of it is not a second fill — it is the real
          `Options_InnerFrame` atlas member, placed below.
        - **Close X wears the 1.12 UI-Panel-MinimizeButton art at the era seat** — which IS the
          era's own close button: 1.15's UIPanelCloseButtonNoScripts names the same four
          Interface\Buttons\UI-Panel-MinimizeButton-* files (Classic SharedUIPanelTemplates.xml
          l.172-180), TOPRIGHT (+4,+4), 32x32. No divergence here at all.
        - **Tabs are STATIC MinimalTab plates** (slice B): Game wears the selected state
          permanently, AddOns the unselected gold — the era swaps these in code
          (MinimalTabMixin), and with nothing behind AddOns the selection can never change, so
          the two states are authored rather than driven. The mixin port comes with the addon
          list. Width is era's text+40 law via an OnUpdate measure poll; the era's
          measure-at-the-medium-font quirk is deliberately dropped (~6 units of padding).
        - **Search filters nothing yet** — the box takes text, shows/hides its "Search"
          placeholder and clear-X; wiring it to the category/row filter comes with the pages
          slice.
        - **No scroll bars**: the static category tree (9 rows, 2 headers) fits its 199px column
          outright, and the page body is empty. MinimalScrollBar arrives with the pages.
        - Era rows this slice does not ship: the Accessibility group, and Languages/Network under
          System — pages with no benilla knobs behind them yet (0950's "only rows backed by real
          knobs" rule). Nameplates joined in slice B (real nameplate knobs exist to back its
          page).
        - **The window rides a scale knob** (slice B): fonts ride frame scale engine-wide now
          (the 0219 §2 divergence closed), so ERA_WINDOW_SCALE × the era checkFit shrink
          (UIPanelUpdateScaleForFit, transcribed in this file) sizes the whole window; 0.78 is
          the director's-eye starting point, live-tunable. The knob is SHARED: it stands in for
          the era client's UIParent scale (smaller than our 1.12 768-canvas on modern screens),
          so every era-shaped window wears it — GameMenuFrame.xml reads it in its OnShow.
    -->

    <!-- The two era fonts this window needs beyond Fonts.xml's 1.12 set (the era
         GameFontHighlightMedium / GameFontHighlightHuge — Blizzard_Fonts_Shared: FRIZQT 14 and
         20, white). Named Options* rather than the era names on purpose: Fonts.xml is the
         COMPLETE 1.12 set and stays that way; these are this window's own, defined with
         MasterFont's exact shadow inlined (its only content — Fonts.xml l.62). -->
    <Font name="OptionsFontHighlightMedium" font="Fonts\FRIZQT__.TTF" virtual="true">
        <Shadow>
            <Offset><AbsDimension x="1" y="-1"/></Offset>
            <Color r="0" g="0" b="0"/>
        </Shadow>
        <FontHeight><AbsValue val="14"/></FontHeight>
        <Color r="1.0" g="1.0" b="1.0"/>
    </Font>
    <Font name="OptionsFontHighlightHuge" font="Fonts\FRIZQT__.TTF" virtual="true">
        <Shadow>
            <Offset><AbsDimension x="1" y="-1"/></Offset>
            <Color r="0" g="0" b="0"/>
        </Shadow>
        <FontHeight><AbsValue val="20"/></FontHeight>
        <Color r="1.0" g="1.0" b="1.0"/>
    </Font>

    <Script><![CDATA[
        -- The static category tree (era Game tab, Classic tocs), in list order. Keys are the row
        -- name suffixes; the visible label doubles as the page title (the era does the same —
        -- Settings.RegisterCategory names both from one string).
        OPTIONS_CATEGORY_KEYS = {
            "Controls", "Interface", "ActionBars", "Combat", "Social", "Keybindings", "Nameplates",
            "Graphics", "Audio",
        }

        -- The era-window scale (shared, director-owned — the 0219 WORLDMAP_WINDOWED_SCALE
        -- pattern): the era client's UIParent draws smaller against the screen than our 1.12
        -- 768-canvas does on modern displays, and this knob is that mapping — every era-shaped
        -- window wears it (this window here; GameMenuFrame in its OnShow — in the era both draw
        -- at the SAME UIParent px-per-unit, the parity the director's eye checked). At 1.0 the
        -- 724-tall window fills ~85% of the screen's height in our 768-virtual space, where the
        -- reference at typical resolutions reads nearer two-thirds.
        ERA_WINDOW_SCALE = 0.78

        function OptionsFrame_UpdateScale()
            -- The era panel is registered `checkFit = 1`: the panel manager also shrinks it to
            -- fit a small screen (UIPanelUpdateScaleForFit: min over width/height ratios
            -- against the panel + 20 units of air each way, capped at 1) — transcribed here.
            local k = ERA_WINDOW_SCALE
            local wFit = GetScreenWidth() / 940
            local hFit = GetScreenHeight() / 744
            if wFit < k then k = wFit end
            if hFit < k then k = hFit end
            OptionsFrame:SetScale(k)
        end

        -- The era tab width law (MinimalTab.lua l.7): label width + 40. Era measures at OnLoad;
        -- our measure round-trip answers a frame late, so OnUpdate polls until the width is real
        -- (the chat-header converge idiom), then latches. Deliberate divergence: the era
        -- measures with the MEDIUM font it is about to swap away (an accident of its code
        -- order, ~6 units of extra padding); we measure the small font the label actually
        -- wears.
        function OptionsTab_FitWidth(tab)
            if tab.fitted then return end
            local w = getglobal(tab:GetName() .. "Text"):GetStringWidth()
            if w and w > 0 then
                tab:SetWidth(w + 40)
                tab.fitted = true
            end
        end

        -- Each row's OnLoad: remember the key + title, paint the label. The whole row identity
        -- lives here so adding a category is one XML row + one key in the table above.
        function OptionsCategoryRow_OnLoad(row, key, label)
            row.categoryKey = key
            row.pageTitle = label
            row:SetText(label)
        end

        -- The selection: exactly one row wears options_list_active + a white label; everyone
        -- else drops back to bare + gold (the era CategoryList mixin's SetCategoryActive, cut to
        -- our static list). Also writes the page title — the page BODY stays empty this slice.
        function OptionsFrame_SelectCategory(key)
            OptionsFrame.selectedCategory = key
            for _, k in ipairs(OPTIONS_CATEGORY_KEYS) do
                local row = getglobal("OptionsFrameCategoryListRow" .. k)
                local bg = getglobal("OptionsFrameCategoryListRow" .. k .. "Bg")
                if k == key then
                    bg:SetAtlas("Options_List_Active", true)
                    row:SetTextFontObject("GameFontHighlight")
                    OptionsFrameContainerTitle:SetText(row.pageTitle)
                else
                    bg:SetTexture(nil)
                    row:SetTextFontObject("GameFontNormal")
                end
            end
        end
    ]]></Script>

    <!-- The red panel button (era UIPanelButtonTemplate seat, 96x22): GameMenuButtonTemplate's
         four-state UI-Panel-Button art + white/white/grey label trio, copied at this window's
         size (GameMenuFrame.xml l.145 is the shared original; templates don't cross files). -->
    <Button name="OptionsRedButtonTemplate" virtual="true">
        <Size><AbsDimension x="96" y="22"/></Size>
        <ButtonText name="$parentText"/>
        <NormalTexture file="Interface\Buttons\UI-Panel-Button-Up"><TexCoords left="0" right="0.625" top="0" bottom="0.6875"/></NormalTexture>
        <PushedTexture file="Interface\Buttons\UI-Panel-Button-Down"><TexCoords left="0" right="0.625" top="0" bottom="0.6875"/></PushedTexture>
        <DisabledTexture file="Interface\Buttons\UI-Panel-Button-Disabled"><TexCoords left="0" right="0.625" top="0" bottom="0.6875"/></DisabledTexture>
        <HighlightTexture file="Interface\Buttons\UI-Panel-Button-Highlight" alphaMode="ADD"><TexCoords left="0" right="0.625" top="0" bottom="0.6875"/></HighlightTexture>
        <NormalFont inherits="GameFontHighlight"/>
        <HighlightFont inherits="GameFontHighlight"/>
        <DisabledFont inherits="GameFontDisable"/>
    </Button>

    <!-- One category row (era Blizzard_CategoryList.xml's category button): the template's
         175 width is never rendered in the era either — the ScrollBox stretches every row to
         the scroll target's width, 199 with no scroll bar (CategoryList.lua l.176-197 +
         ScrollBoxViewUtil), and ours is the no-bar case. Gold label centered in the row (the
         full-row box below); a
         CENTER bg that is EMPTY until the hover/selected atlas lands on it (options_list_hover
         / options_list_active at atlas size — 187x21, centered: 6 units in from either edge of
         the 199 row, the alignment the first cut's 175-wide rows broke). Selection is
         OptionsFrame_SelectCategory's; hover only ever paints a row that is NOT the selection. -->
    <Button name="OptionsCategoryRowTemplate" virtual="true">
        <Size><AbsDimension x="199" y="20"/></Size>
        <Layers>
            <Layer level="BACKGROUND">
                <Texture name="$parentBg">
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="CENTER"/></Anchors>
                </Texture>
            </Layer>
        </Layers>
        <!-- The era label is a box spanning the WHOLE row — TOPLEFT (36,+1) AND BOTTOMRIGHT
             (0,+1), era CategoryList.xml l.72-77 — so the default MIDDLE vertical justify
             CENTERS the text in the 20-tall row (1 unit high of true center, the era's own
             nudge). The first cut had only the TOPLEFT corner: the auto-sized label hung from
             the row TOP, ~4 units high of center ("text not vertically centered" — director,
             2026-08-04). justifyH LEFT is the era's own attribute; a full-row box without it
             would center horizontally. -->
        <ButtonText name="$parentText" justifyH="LEFT">
            <Anchors>
                <Anchor point="TOPLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="36" y="1"/></Offset></Anchor>
                <Anchor point="BOTTOMRIGHT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="0" y="1"/></Offset></Anchor>
            </Anchors>
        </ButtonText>
        <NormalFont inherits="GameFontNormal"/>
        <HighlightFont inherits="GameFontNormal"/>
        <DisabledFont inherits="GameFontDisable"/>
        <Scripts>
            <OnClick>OptionsFrame_SelectCategory(this.categoryKey)</OnClick>
            <OnEnter>
                if OptionsFrame.selectedCategory ~= this.categoryKey then
                    getglobal(this:GetName() .. "Bg"):SetAtlas("Options_List_Hover", true)
                end
            </OnEnter>
            <OnLeave>
                if OptionsFrame.selectedCategory ~= this.categoryKey then
                    getglobal(this:GetName() .. "Bg"):SetTexture(nil)
                end
            </OnLeave>
        </Scripts>
    </Button>

    <!-- A category group header (era SettingsCategoryListHeaderTemplate, stretched to the 199
         row width like the rows): a 14px white label at LEFT (20,-1) over the group's
         BACKGROUND WASH — the Options_CategoryHeader_<n> atlas the era Init pins at the
         header's TOPLEFT at atlas size (199x144: a header band whose gradient runs down over
         the group's own rows; the rows' hover/selected plates draw above it, being later
         siblings). The <n> cycles per header (CategoryList.lua l.378-384) — each instance's
         OnLoad passes its own. -->
    <Frame name="OptionsCategoryHeaderTemplate" virtual="true">
        <Size><AbsDimension x="199" y="30"/></Size>
        <Layers>
            <Layer level="ARTWORK">
                <Texture name="$parentBg">
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="TOPLEFT"/></Anchors>
                </Texture>
            </Layer>
            <Layer level="OVERLAY">
                <FontString name="$parentLabel" inherits="OptionsFontHighlightMedium">
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="LEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="20" y="-1"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
                </FontString>
            </Layer>
        </Layers>
    </Frame>

    <Frame name="OptionsFrame" frameStrata="HIGH" enableMouse="true" hidden="true">
        <Size><AbsDimension x="920" y="724"/></Size>
        <Anchors><Anchor point="CENTER"/></Anchors>
        <Layers>
            <Layer level="BACKGROUND">
                <!-- FlatPanelBackgroundTemplate as one fill (header SCOPE note: the era tints
